## 6. Cost Optimization Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph COMPUTE["⚡ COMPUTE OPTIMIZATION"]
        SLOT[Slot Reservations\n3yr CUD = 35% off\nBaseline: 2000 slots]
        AUTOSCALE[Autoscaling\nMin: 500, Max: 5000]
        SPOT[Spot VMs\nDataproc Workers\n60-90% savings]
        FLEX[Flex Slots\nOn-demand burst\nPer-second billing]
    end

    subgraph STORAGE["💾 STORAGE OPTIMIZATION"]
        PART[Partition by Date\nPrune 90%+ data]
        CLUSTER[Cluster by High-Card\ncustomer_id, session_id]
        COMPRESS[ZSTD Compression\n30-50% size reduction]
        LIFECYCLE[Lifecycle Rules\n90d → Nearline, 365d → Coldline]
    end

    subgraph QUERY["🔍 QUERY OPTIMIZATION"]
        MV[Materialized Views\nTop 20 Aggregations\nAuto-refresh]
        BI[BI Engine\n100GB reserved\nSub-second dashboards]
        CACHE[Query Result Cache\n24hr TTL, free reuse]
        PRUNE[Partition Pruning\nWHERE event_date >= ...]
    end

    subgraph MONITORING["📊 COST MONITORING"]
        BUDGET[Budget Alerts\n50%/80%/100% thresholds]
        LABEL[Labels: env, team, project\nCost allocation]
        RECOMMEND[Recommender API\nSlot, storage, query insights]
        REPORT[Monthly Chargeback\nPer team/project]
    end

    SLOT --> AUTOSCALE
    AUTOSCALE --> FLEX
    SPOT -.-> DATAPROC[Dataproc Clusters]

    PART --> CLUSTER
    CLUSTER --> COMPRESS
    COMPRESS --> LIFECYCLE

    MV --> BI
    BI --> CACHE
    CACHE --> PRUNE

    BUDGET --> LABEL
    LABEL --> RECOMMEND
    RECOMMEND --> REPORT

    classDef compute fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2
    classDef storage fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#388e3c
    classDef query fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#f57c00
    classDef monitor fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#7b1fa2

    class SLOT,AUTOSCALE,SPOT,FLEX compute
    class PART,CLUSTER,COMPRESS,LIFECYCLE storage
    class MV,BI,CACHE,PRUNE query
